{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion (config_045) achieves 0.725 acc, far exceeding scgpt-based configs (~0.52-0.54). However, we lack an rna_only baseline for scvi_n200 to determine whether the image modality actually contributes complementary information. With scgpt, image added only ~1% (0.411→0.422), suggesting it may be redundant. Question: config_051 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) directly compares to config_045 with the image encoder and fusion removed, isolating the image's marginal contribution. Why this is best: This is the most fundamental remaining architectural question. If rna_only approaches 0.725, the image is redundant and future budget should focus on RNA representation; if it drops substantially, the multimodal design is justified and fusion/image-encoder optimizations become worthwhile. This single experiment resolves a high-uncertainty design decision that would redirect all subsequent experiments."
}

